Imports:
  - Types:
      - BillingApi
      - BillingDependencies
      - BillingPurchaseResult
      - BillingProduct
      - BillingResponseCode
    From: core/util/src/main/java/org/signal/core/util/billing

Annotations: |
  This cell is the concrete, Google-Play-specific implementation of the `BillingApi` extension
  point declared in core/util/billing. `BillingFactory` is the runtime switch: it returns a
  real `BillingApiImpl` when the feature is enabled, or the interface's own Empty no-op
  otherwise, so callers never need to branch on availability themselves.

---

"BillingApi::BillingApiImpl(billingDependencies: BillingDependencies)":
  location: BillingApiImpl.kt
  annotations: |
    Implements `BillingApi` against Google Play's Billing Client library.

    `billingDependencies`: supplies application context and product/plan identifiers, per
    `BillingDependencies` from Imports.

    Algorithm:
    1. Lazily establish and cache a connection to the platform billing service; every public
       method waits for a connected (or definitively failed) connection before proceeding.
    2. Cache queried product details for a bounded period rather than re-querying on every call.
    3. Translate the platform library's own response/purchase-state codes into this app's
       `BillingResponseCode`/`BillingPurchaseResult` from Imports before returning to callers.
  methods:
    "getBillingPurchaseResults() -> stream:Flow<BillingPurchaseResult>": |
      Implements the `BillingApi` method from Imports; backed by an internal hot flow fed by the
      platform library's purchase-update listener.
    "queryProduct() -> product:BillingProduct?": |
      Implements the `BillingApi` method from Imports, returning a `BillingProduct` (or none if
      pricing is unavailable) using the cached-or-fresh product-details query described in the
      type-level Algorithm.
    "queryPurchases() -> result:BillingPurchaseResult": |
      Implements the `BillingApi` method from Imports.
    "launchBillingFlow(activity: Activity)": |
      Implements the `BillingApi` method from Imports. If an active, auto-renewing purchase
      already exists, immediately reports it instead of opening the purchase UI again.
    "getApiAvailability() -> code:BillingResponseCode": |
      Implements the `BillingApi` method from Imports.

"BillingFactory()":
  location: BillingFactory.kt
  annotations: |
    Selects which `BillingApi` implementation the rest of the app receives, so the choice is made
    in exactly one place.
  methods:
    "create(billingDependencies: BillingDependencies, isBackupsAvailable: Boolean) -> api:BillingApi": |
      Returns a `BillingApiImpl` wired to `billingDependencies` when `isBackupsAvailable` is
      true, or the Empty singleton from `BillingApi`'s Imports declaration otherwise.

      `isBackupsAvailable`: whether the paid-backups feature (the only current consumer of
      billing) is enabled for this build/account.

